  "paraphrased_content": "The union of Princess Märtha Louise of Norway and Durek Verrett, a self-proclaimed shaman from California, took place on Saturday in an unconventional royal ceremony. Despite the non-traditional nature of the event, crowds gathered in the rainy streets of Geiranger, hoping to see the bride. As the sole daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja, the 52-year-old princess holds the fourth position in the Norwegian line of succession. The wedding, held in a traditional Norwegian church at the Hotel Union near the Geiranger fjord, was attended by royalty and celebrities alike. Princess Märtha Louise was accompanied by seven bridesmaids, including her daughters Leah and Emma Behn from her previous marriage to the late author Ari Behn, which ended in divorce in 2017. Notable guests included her brother, Crown Prince Haakon, and his wife, Crown Princess Mette-Marit, as well as Sweden’s Crown Princess Victoria with Prince Daniel, and Prince Constantijn and Princess Laurentien of the Netherlands. Known for her unconventional lifestyle, Princess Märtha Louise has identified as a clairvoyant and once operated a school focused on spiritual healing and angelic communication. In 2022, she announced her decision to step back from royal duties to concentrate on her business ventures with Verrett, aiming to separate their activities from the Norwegian royal family. Verrett, who refers to himself as a 'servant of God' and 'energy activator' on social media, counts Gwyneth Paltrow among his clients, describing her as a 'soul sister.'"
